# Fixed 2026-10-03, panel 187's R5 (V5, built by the sitting's compiler
# engineer and widened by lane rec187's first pass): the shape `g2/r09`
# beside defect 130. Symptom: a declaration whose body is missing is told at
# the next line, the convention of every missing body, and the message named
# only the kind, *a `function` needs an indented body*, its excerpt under
# another declaration that has its body, `function main()`. Cause: the
# owner handed to the body's reader was the keyword's phrase alone. A head
# read up to its name hands that name on: *the `function` `f` needs an
# indented body*, a constant by its name and a test by its title, at the top
# level and among a record's fields, and where the signature or the type
# failed after the name was read. Codes and places stand.

record Q
    x: i64
    function f() -> i64  #~ expected_field

#~v missing_body
function main()
    print(1)

record Two
    x: i64
    function f() -> i64  #~ expected_field
    function g()  #~ missing_body

#~v missing_body
function before_another() -> i64

#~v missing_body
function a_signature_that_failed(x i64) -> i64  #~ expected_parameter_type

#~v missing_body
constant LIMIT: i64

#~v missing_body
test "a title"

#~v missing_body
function last() -> i64  #~v missing_body
